{"text": "nineteen", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>From Middle English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">nynetene</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">nintene</i>, from Old English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"ang\">ni\u0121ont\u012bene</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"ang\">ni\u0121ont\u0113ne</i>, from Proto-Germanic <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"gem-pro\">*newuntehun</i>. Cognate with Dutch <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"nl\">negentien</i>, Low German <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"nds\">negenteihn</i>, Hunsrik <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"hrx\">neinzen</i>, German <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"de\">neunzehn</i>, Danish <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"da\">nitten</i>.\n</p><p>Equivalent to <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">nine</i> +\u200e <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">-teen</i>\n</p>", "pos": []}], "pronunciation": [["Received Pronunciation", "/\u02c8na\u026anti\u02d0n/"], ["Received Pronunciation", "/na\u026an\u02c8ti\u02d0n/"], ["General American", "/\u02ccna\u026an\u02c8tin/"], ["General American", "/\u02c8na\u026an\u02cctin/"]]}